### Next: Manual E2E Testing (T23)

E2E Acceptance scenarios from requirements.md:
1. exit in attached session → gone <1s
2. exit in unattached session → gone <1s
3. UI kill → gone, exactly one session-removed, daemon+process group dead
4. kill -9 daemon → gone <1s
5. 5 sessions with sleep 999; restart → 5 back before first API response, sleeps alive
6. Sever watch connection while daemon PID alive → unreachable shown, NOT removed, recovers on reconnect
7. Kill A, create A immediately → old callbacks don't touch new A
8. chmod 000 socket dir 30s → zero removals
9. Remove session; switch groups, reload, toggle WS → no resurrection, no duplicate groups, pane tree/pool cleaned
10. Remote peer session attach/kill/file-open → unchanged
11. Pre-upgrade daemon → adopted, exit detected
12. Stale lifecycle files → cleaned at boot
13. Server up: create/list via API; server down: direct spawn + scan fallback, adoption picks up at next boot
14. WS reconnect with empty snapshot → all local pruned (list, panes, pool, groups); failed fetch → nothing pruned, filters intact


